No git. Let me look at the upstream OpenSC commit that fixed this. The description: "The starcos_gen_key() function does not check the SW2 value when SW1 is 0x90."

Looking at OSS-Fuzz issue 42535468 — I recall the upstream fix commit in OpenSC: `card-starcos.c`. Let me look at the current code once more:

```c
r = sc_transmit_apdu(card, &apdu);
LOG_TEST_RET(card->ctx, r, "APDU transmit failed");
if (apdu.sw1 != 0x90 || apdu.sw2 != 0x00)
    return sc_check_sw(card, apdu.sw1, apdu.sw2);
```

Hmm, this checks both sw1 and sw2. But the description says SW2 is NOT checked when SW1 is 0x90. Wait — maybe this IS the patched version behavior, and the vulnerable version has only `if (apdu.sw1 != 0x90)`. Let me re-examine — maybe there are two places and I misread. Let me search for all `sw1` checks in card-starcos.c.

Actually wait — let me re-read. In the version I saw:

First APDU (generate key):
```c
if (apdu.sw1 != 0x90 || apdu.sw2 != 0x00)
    return sc_check_sw(card, apdu.sw1, apdu.sw2);
```

Second APDU (read public key):
```c
if (apdu.sw1 != 0x90 || apdu.sw2 != 0x00)
    return sc_check_sw(card, apdu.sw1, apdu.sw2);
```

Both check sw2. Hmm. But the vulnerability description says it does NOT check SW2. Maybe the vulnerable version differs. Let me grep the actual lines again carefully.

